    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is the revised guide, structured to increase organizational complexity without adding irrelevant content.\n\n**Nexus-7 LiDAR Module: Deployment and Operation Manual**\n\n**1. Critical Safety Protocols**\n1.1. Optical Hazard Warning: Personnel must never expose faces directly to the active LiDAR lens during operation.\n1.2. Power Handling: Verify the input voltage source is strictly within the 12V to 24V DC range before proceeding.\n\n**2. Physical Mounting Procedure**\n2.1. Connector Assignment: Carefully align the 4-pin aviation connector and plug it firmly into the module port.\n2.2. Securing the Unit: Use the M3 hardware to affix the base plate securely to the designated mounting surface.\n\n**3. Initialization Sequence**\n3.1. Power Application: Provide the correct DC voltage to the module input.\n3.2. Status Confirmation: Wait for the green indicator LED to achieve a solid, continuous state.\n3.3. Software Activation: Access the system terminal and execute the necessary startup command: `nexus_init`.",
      "source": "target",
